# Copy this file to `.env` and paste the key THERE. `.env` is gitignored; THIS FILE IS NOT.
#
# 🔴 THE COPY GOES IN THE REPOSITORY ROOT, NOT NEXT TO THIS FILE, and getting that wrong fails
# SILENTLY. Every module reads the key through one function -- `testing/common.py:load_key()` -- and
# it opens `<repository root>/.env`. A copy made here, in `AGENTIC-ARBITER/`, is read by nothing:
# `serve_live.py` still starts, `/api/health` still answers, and the page's data-source console
# reports "API KEY ON THAT MACHINE: absent" while the key sits in a file one directory down. The
# instruction below used to be `cp .env.example .env`, which from this directory produces exactly
# that -- and it was invisible on the machine it was written on, because both files existed there.
#
#   cd <the repository root>
#   cp AGENTIC-ARBITER/.env.example .env      # then edit ./.env , never this file
#
# NEVER put a real credential in this file. `.gitignore` deliberately re-includes this template
# (`!.env.example`) so it stays visible to collaborators, which means anything written here
# WOULD be committed.
FORTYGUARD_API_KEY=

# Nothing else here is secret. NOAA ASOS (via Iowa State) and the OpenStreetMap Overpass API are
# both free and keyless, which is why the weather and geometry layers work with no credential at all.
